# .no-backup — gitignored paths that deliberately have no backup, and WHY.
# Read by hygiene-check.py. Anything ignored and NOT listed here gets reported.
# One path prefix per line, then the reason. A reason is the point: "it is noisy" is not one.
#
# Also supports:  BACKED-UP  <path>  <YYYY-MM-DD>  <where>   for paths that ARE copied by hand.

.env.local     holds Vercel credentials (a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN and project linkage). Credentials do
               not go on an unencrypted stick that travels — Set A rule 1, Set C rule C5. This is
               deliberately unrecoverable: regenerate it with `vercel env pull`, which is the whole
               reason it must not be backed up rather than a gap in the backups.
.build/        test and build output, regenerated by `npm run build` / the test run.
